    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10841" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνυμφος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not bridal,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. τροφή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1183
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυμφη ἄ.</span> a bride
				<i>that is no bride, unhappy</i> bride, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				612
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				547
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				548
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>without bride</i> or <i>mistress,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλαθρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1125
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				4301
			</span></i>.</div>
